At Thu, 4 May 2006 13:59:17 +0100,
techie tone wrote:
> 
> what is the return value of "snd_pcm_avail_update".
> 
> Is it the no. of bytes available with the driver?
> Is it no. of samples available?

Neither.  It's "frames" in ALSA term.

1 frame = #channels * sample-bytes.
In the case of 2-channel 16bit PCM, 1 frame corresponds to 4 bytes.

All parameters using snd_pcm_[su]frames_t in alsa-lib are represented
in frames.


